<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador bank liquidity up 0.31 pct at June 13.</title>
<headline>Ecuador bank liquidity up 0.31 pct at June 13.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's Central Bank said Thursday liquidity in the banking system grew 0.31 percent or 62 million sucres to 19.89 billion sucres in the week to June 13.</p>
<p>At the end of May, bank liquidity stood at 19.61 billion sucres.</p>
<p>Total liquidity in the bank sector at the end of 1996 was 16.99 billion sucres, up 35.8 percent from 1995.</p>
<p>((--Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433, e-mail: reuters1@reutersecu.com.ec))</p>
